Design for  Embedded Disassembly Process strategy integrates the disassembly process inside a product during manufacturing and activate it at disassembly. This design strategy creates products that are self-disassemblable and the process can be activated through a clear movement (for customer disassembly) or a mechanical movement (for industrial disassembly).

Designers should attempt to:
• identifying the essential part of currently used disassembly process and minimizing the mechanism for disassembly and then embedding them into the products;
• for multiple product lifecycles, it should be possible to reinsert the mechanism multiple times;
• If the product contains hazardous materials, the mechanism should be hidden to customers;  
